    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC CA-24-059: Oak Gardens, located at 795 Willow Road in Menlo Park, requested and is being recommended for a reservation of $2,500,000 in annual federal tax credits and $3,247,634 in total state tax credits to finance the new construction of 60 units of housing serving special needs tenants with rents affordable to households earning 30%-50% of area median income (AMI).",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001645"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MidPen's February 2026 property profile lists unit sizes of 568 sq ft (1BR), 862 sq ft (2BR) and 1,027 sq ft (3BR), and lists the California Tax Credit Allocation Committee among funders.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003379"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Architect's project page lists completion as Spring 2026, construction cost estimated at $35M, LEED Gold, all-electric building with a photovoltaic array, and a 2.137-acre site.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003381"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Palo Alto Daily Post (Feb 27, 2025): $35 million construction cost; completion and opening expected spring 2026.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-003380"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "County parcel layer owner names for APN 062-470-090: MP Oak Gardens Associates LP lessee, United States of America, and State of California Dept of Housing and (field truncated).",
      "src": [
        "SRC-000918"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SF YIMBY, Nov. 21, 2026: the official grand opening ceremony has been held; 62 permanent supportive units for veterans and their families.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-004290"
      ]
    }
